# Bird

A separate model. Do not touch `Human`, `BalanceController`, or the
`HeadlessTrial` stand.

Layer: body `Bird`, actuators `Muscle` / `JointFriction` (ragdoll only),
flight `BirdFlight` + drag `BodyAero`, sensor `BirdSensors`,
control `BirdController`. Who sets `mode` (the brain) is
`.cursor/rules/ai.mdc`; this file is flap and landing physics, not
behavior.

## Handshake with agent `ai`

Colleague: profile `ai`, law `.cursor/rules/ai.mdc`. They write **what**
the bird wants. This profile writes **how** the body flies.

| | Agent `ai` | Agent `bird` (this file) |
|---|---|---|
| Writes | `mode` / `SetFacing` (`BirdDrive`, `BirdWander`, `BirdFlockDrive`) | lift, flap, `walkThrust`, PD, perch, pose |
| Must not write | `AddForce`, `BirdFlight` formula, `flapFrequency` | `FactionMember`, vision/hearing, fear of a human |
| Sensors | world see/hear (own layer, later) | `BirdSensors` — inner ear and feet, not eyes |

Do not invent `BirdIntent`, `Vision`, `Hearing`, or `FactionMember` here.

`takeoffDelay` Stand→Fly is a **demo timer**, not the brain. Flock
landing in `TickFlock` may set `mode = Sit` and zero the delay —
that is contact rest, not faction. `BirdDrive` (card `BIRD-2`) decides
in `Update`; it must not fight the landing write in the same physics
step (`sitHold` after touchdown).

Flock eye origin later is the **body** (`headVisual` has no
`Rigidbody2D`). Ragdoll eye origin is `Head`. Facing is
`BirdController.facing` (±1): ahead is that sign along X, not a street
left/right. Do not use `CameraFollow` or `Light2D` as sight.

Turn (flock): do **not** `localScale` the `Rigidbody2D` / perch and do
**not** rotate the body 180° (legs would point at the sky). Put neck,
wings, tail, legs under `Look` and set `lookRoot.localScale.x = facing`.
Thrust heading is `Rot(pitch) * (facing, 0)`; pitch goal is
`target * facing` (+8° right, −8° left). Walk thrust uses the same sign.
Ragdoll stay +X until a card. CLI: `-birdFacing` / `-birdTurnAfter`.
Play: `Bird` / `BirdFlock50` default `birdDriveKind` wander (BIRD-3 / BIRD-4).
Prey stoop stays `birdDriveKind` prey. Sit pitch is 0 (not the 12° flare).
Facing flip softens pitch spring 0.4 s — wander turns ±X in the air.
`BirdWander` now enters Glide `glideLead` before fly ends (agent `ai`).
BIRD-5: dirt is not home — the brain writes Fly toward `homeX`. This
profile still Sit+Settle on contact in `TickFlock` (one physics step);
the brain overwrites dirt on the next `Update`. Enable the perch and
the glide flare when `PlantTree.NearPerch`, not only when height above
flat dirt is < 0.45 m (a twig is higher). Facing-flip soft pitch does
not extend if already in the 0.4 s window — Glide may chatter ±X at
the slot.
Visual (agent `visual`, 30.08): Look mirror is enough — capsules/ellipse
are symmetric, no new texture. Keep `DimFar` / sorting after the flip
(near wing stays bright and in front). Do not move `Body/Visual` under
`Look` until a directed albedo exists.

Two builds:

| `BirdRig` | Where | Bodies |
|---|---|---|
| `Ragdoll` | stance stand (`-bird` without `-birdRig flock`) | joints and muscles |
| `Flock` | scene, flock | **one** `Rigidbody2D`; wings and legs are look |

Dozens of birds in a scene — `Flock` only. A ragdoll per individual
gives ~16 bodies.
Flock: one `FixedUpdate` (`BirdController` calls `sensors.Tick` → pose
cache → `flight.Tick`).
Wing and leg look is `LateUpdate`, not a physics step.
Above `skipProbeAboveHeight` (0.5 m) the flock does not call `OverlapBox`,
unless `PlantTree.NearPerch` — a tree branch is higher than flat ground,
and Sit still needs a foot read. `treeSupport` is grounded + NearPerch +
height > 0.35 m above dirt stance — the AABB alone counts soil under
the stump as a perch. The brain reads `treeSupport` for BIRD-5, not
raw `NearPerch`. Plant seats Play birds via
`PlantTree.SeatBirds`; this profile keeps perch pose and pitch. Headless
flat wander does not spawn trees.
Wood is ghost to a bird (`Bird.GhostTreeWood`): the body flies through
the crown. Sit contact is only `BirdPerch` pads at `GetPerchSlots`,
not the trunk collider. Do not add a second Rigidbody2D per pad.
Flock look has no `HumanSegment` on the feathers: the component is only
on the body.

Lift is one force on the body in `BirdFlight`. The flap is a switch:
Fly gives thrust in time with the flap; without a flap the force is
zero. Glide is lift ~ v², stall at low speed. In flight and on descent
the body holds pitch with a spring; near the ground — a nose-up flash.
Enable the support (`perchCollider`) before impact, or it lands on the
chest and tumbles. Body drag is computed by the same `BirdFlight`
(`BodyAero.Apply`); there is no second `FixedUpdate` per individual.
The stand writes bird summary fields `wallPerSim`,
`applied.rigidbodyCount`, `continuousBodyCount`, `muscleBehaviourCount`,
`frictionBehaviourCount`, `meanProbeHits`, `humanSegmentCount` — a cost
ruler, not a flight tune.

Flock landing: `-stopFlap` switches to `Glide` (not `Stand`). Like a
stone — `-stopFlapMode stand`. Liftoff counts only above
`takeoffClearance`; otherwise Fly near the ground lands immediately.
After contact the pitch spring stays — otherwise support friction
spins the body. Flock walk is a look step + `walkThrust` thrust with
a `walkSpeed` cap.

Paired limbs: anchors with no X spread, look is `SetVisualOffset`.
Play spawn: scene `Assets/Scenes/Bird.unity` (`humanCount = 0`,
`birdCount = 1`, `cameraFollowsBird`). Do not open `World` /
`SampleScene` for flight.
Flock Play is scene `BirdFlock50`, not `Bird` and not `World`.
Hens: same `Bird` class, `BirdKind.Chicken`. Play scene `Chicken`.
Crow is the flying canon. Chicken is heavier, short-winged,
`hoverMean` 0.55 — a hop, not a cruise. Stance Y after `ApplyKind`.
CLI `-birdKind chicken`.
Every kind has a `Beak` segment (card `BIRD-8-beak`). Ragdoll: hinge
on the head. Flock: look child + trigger, no extra `Rigidbody2D`.
Hits go through `BeakStrike` only — not a wing, not the chest.
Stand: `run-trial.ps1 -Rebuild -Duration 10 -Label bird_stand -Extra @('-bird','1')`.
Without `-bird` the human path does not change. `-takeoffDelay 0` —
stance without takeoff. `-birdMode fly` — flap and thrust.
`-birdRig flock` — flock build. `-stopFlap 4` — drop the flap at the
4th second (glide by default). `-stopFlapMode glide|stand`.
`-walkThrust` — flock step. `-birdFacing 1|-1`. `-birdTurnAfter`.
`-birdMode sit|attack`. Play drive: `birdDrive` on `Bird` / `BirdFlock50`.

## Budget (optimization 02.09)

Read `Trials/Runs/opt_bird_code_02.md` and `opt_agent_proposals.md`
(section bird). Not a GO card. PERF-5 is closed.

Flock N=50 at 200 Hz is the **solver edge** (`wallPerSim ≈ 1`), not
empty `FixedUpdate` and not `NearPerch`. One ragdoll is 17 RB / 32
muscles / 16 frictions — hero budget, stance stand only.

Do not:

- Cut `flapFrequency`, `aiStride`, or 200 Hz for FPS.
- Move `BirdFlight.Tick` to `Update`.
- Disable driven `BirdSensors` / `BirdFlight` again (0% on two repeats).
- Spawn ragdoll birds in `BirdFlock50` or World (`birdCount = 0`).
- Replace the foot probe with `GetContacts` while `probeSat` is 0.

Perch lab already answered the optional probe card:
`perf_flock_metric_tree1` — `probeSaturatedFraction` **0**,
`meanProbeHits` 0.54, 3774 probes / 20 s. Keep `OverlapBoxNonAlloc`
and the cruise skip. `NearPerch` stays one AABB; sensors cache
`nearPerch` once per tick.
